														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2048853">
									

<p>I also found there to be a tonal disconnect between the language used in the sign-off message, the show description, and the rest of the piece. The episode descriptions are gloriously bizarre (Thatcher was particularly unsettling), the conceit is compelling (anomalous broadcast), but this &quot;fun&quot; language is just out of place. If the intended effect is to convince the reader that the things responsible are inhuman, well, that's <em>abundantly clear</em> from the broadcast content. The altered language just creates a spike in silliness where one isn't really appropriate, especially since the host seems perfectly capable of normal speech.</p>
<p>As said above:</p>
