			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2048863">
									

<p>I noticed you wrote a lot of the documentation with the Foundation seeming to have absolute knowledge of the thing. For example:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>it mimics art from other television series, allowing it to attract more viewers mistaking it for another program.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Maybe if it read as a researcher's speculation rather than an outright fact.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>only seen from the neck down, making identification impossible</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Does it make it <em>impossible</em>?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The general consensus among researchers assigned to SCP-2030 is that victims are likely abducted after their use in the show, with their disappearances covered up when possible <strong>through the use of an anomalous disinformation distribution agent</strong>.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I don't see what this does for the article. It says a bit too much and now I'm wondering where they got to the conclusion of anomalous disinformation distribution agent. It's a speculation about a speculation.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>We hunger. We hunger.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I thought the addendum was enough, this is extremely cliched. Definitely not an &quot;I SEE YOU&quot; that might make me feel like I'm involved. Not quite a stinger.</p>
<p>But this gets a +1 because I would keep reading if this was the first article I saw and the fantastic imagery in the addendum.</p>

							</div>

								
					
